## Idempotency keys

A client that may retry a write (a payment, an order) sends a unique
`Idempotency-Key` header, the same on every retry of that one operation. The
first request runs; a retry gets the stored answer with
`Idempotent-Replayed: true`. A retry while the first still runs gets 409, the
same key with a different body 422. 5xx answers are not kept, so the client
can retry those for real. Keys are per caller (`Authorization` header) and
last 24 hours, in the `idempotency_keys` table.
